# poc/*.json and poc/data.js are BUILD OUTPUT of tools/build_json.py + tools/extract_*.py,
# regenerated in full from examples/CaseStudies/*.md by `./run.sh build`. They are tracked so
# the frontend team can read a snapshot without running the pipeline, but they must never be
# the reason a merge or rebase stops.
#
# They caused four separate pull failures between 2026-08-08 and 2026-08-11 -- the last one
# stopped a rebase mid-flight, and the pipeline then ran against a half-applied working tree
# and lost a project's Phase 11 (Lessons L10). The content is never worth resolving by hand:
# whichever side is kept, `./run.sh build` immediately reproduces the correct file from the
# dossiers, which are the real source.
#
# Requires ONE-TIME setup per clone, since git has no built-in "ours" driver for files:
#     git config merge.ours.driver true
# Without it git falls back to a normal conflict, i.e. today's behaviour -- no worse.
poc/cif.json    merge=ours
poc/data.js     merge=ours
poc/*.json      merge=ours
